1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:06,380
THIS PROGRAM CONTAINS
AI-GENERATED CONTENT

2
00:00:06,381 --> 00:00:08,467
YOON JAEMIN

3
00:00:10,219 --> 00:00:12,513
[player] Hey, Lee Hyunsoo!
Think you can catch this?

4
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:29,321
[gasps]

5
00:00:35,911 --> 00:00:38,080
[sobbing]

6
00:00:43,252 --> 00:00:45,754
[theme music playing]

7
00:00:49,216 --> 00:00:52,468
MURDER CLUB: LIAR'S TABLE

8
00:00:52,469 --> 00:00:54,095
Isn't that the director?

9
00:00:54,096 --> 00:00:55,722
[Kang Dohyun] That's him, right?

10
00:00:56,223 --> 00:00:57,431
- Yeah, it is.
- It is.

11
00:00:57,432 --> 00:01:00,601
- Oh jeez, the director…
- He's the culprit.

12
00:01:00,602 --> 00:01:03,479
[Kang Dohyun] What's going on here?
It looks like a family photo.

13
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:05,439
Oh, there are multiple CCTVs.

14
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:06,858
Let's see.

15
00:01:11,655 --> 00:01:14,448
JO HAJUN BUYS A CAKE?

16
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:16,117
To be honest, it caught me off guard.

17
00:01:16,118 --> 00:01:19,370
<i>It happened to be me,
so I turned it off instantly.</i>

18
00:01:19,371 --> 00:01:22,039
But the truth is,
I was the one who ordered the cake.

19
00:01:22,040 --> 00:01:23,291
It was me.

20
00:01:23,292 --> 00:01:27,421
I ordered a special custom cake
with the aim of targeting Park Taeo.

21
00:01:28,171 --> 00:01:30,590
It all lines up. This is conclusive proof.

22
00:01:30,591 --> 00:01:32,675
All right. Director.

23
00:01:32,676 --> 00:01:34,093
- You're back.
- If you look here,

24
00:01:34,094 --> 00:01:36,512
there's a torn-up photo with you in it.

25
00:01:36,513 --> 00:01:38,931
- [Kim Doyun] Can you explain this photo?
- [Kang Dohyun] Look. Right here.

26
00:01:38,932 --> 00:01:41,058
- Can you explain it?
- It's you, isn't it?

27
00:01:41,059 --> 00:01:42,602
- [Jo Hajun] Oh, this.
- Yeah.

28
00:01:42,603 --> 00:01:44,770
It's our parent company.

29
00:01:44,771 --> 00:01:47,690
It's the Geumseong Group chairman
and his family.

30
00:01:47,691 --> 00:01:49,775
- Why did you rip it?
- Why take a photo together?

31
00:01:49,776 --> 00:01:51,444
I don't know if I should say…

32
00:01:51,445 --> 00:01:52,820
Fess up right now!

33
00:01:52,821 --> 00:01:54,196
He's the youngest son of a chaebol family.

34
00:01:54,197 --> 00:01:56,282
Spill, already! Explain this.

35
00:01:56,283 --> 00:01:58,035
- He's a chaebol's son.
- You're the culprit, aren't you?

36
00:01:58,660 --> 00:01:59,744
Don't just laugh.

37
00:01:59,745 --> 00:02:01,495
- Wait.
- You rotten bastard!

38
00:02:01,496 --> 00:02:02,621
Wait, Dohyun.

39
00:02:02,622 --> 00:02:05,082
You're very worked up right now.

40
00:02:05,083 --> 00:02:06,208
He raised his hand.

41
00:02:06,209 --> 00:02:07,335
[Kim Doyun] Hear me out.

42
00:02:07,336 --> 00:02:09,003
- The truth is…
- Yes?

43
00:02:09,004 --> 00:02:12,965
…I'm the director
of the PR Strategy Team, right?

44
00:02:12,966 --> 00:02:15,676
These people are actually

45
00:02:15,677 --> 00:02:17,346
- my family.
- [Kim Doyun] I knew it.

46
00:02:17,929 --> 00:02:19,013
My father's the chairman.

47
00:02:19,014 --> 00:02:20,140
I thought so.

48
00:02:20,766 --> 00:02:22,767
<i>Oh, you're the chairman's son.</i>

49
00:02:22,768 --> 00:02:25,227
JO HAJUN IS THE YOUNGEST SON
OF A CHAEBOL FAMILY

50
00:02:25,228 --> 00:02:26,395
- [Kim Doyun] Director.
- Yes?

51
00:02:26,396 --> 00:02:28,314
It turns out you're the son
of a chaebol family.

52
00:02:28,315 --> 00:02:31,150
But during my private conversation
with Pani earlier… I mean--

53
00:02:31,151 --> 00:02:32,652
- Coach Yoon.
- [Kim Doyun] Okay.

54
00:02:32,653 --> 00:02:35,404
I had a private conversation
with the coach,

55
00:02:35,405 --> 00:02:37,448
and he said you didn't have much motive

56
00:02:37,449 --> 00:02:38,866
for killing Park Taeo.

57
00:02:38,867 --> 00:02:40,618
- Why kill someone for a canceled advert?
- Right.

58
00:02:40,619 --> 00:02:41,994
- That's what the coach said.
- Yeah.

59
00:02:41,995 --> 00:02:43,162
Do you agree with that?

60
00:02:43,163 --> 00:02:46,916
Of course, you shouldn't kill someone
over a canceled advert.

61
00:02:46,917 --> 00:02:49,085
But based on the information I have,

62
00:02:49,086 --> 00:02:52,088
the promotion campaign
was career-defining for you

63
00:02:52,089 --> 00:02:55,591
and played a major role
in your performance evaluation,

64
00:02:55,592 --> 00:02:59,887
<i>so it was a key factor
in deciding the succession.</i>

65
00:02:59,888 --> 00:03:01,764
So if this campaign fell through,

66
00:03:01,765 --> 00:03:03,057
he would be ruined.

67
00:03:03,058 --> 00:03:05,267
- For failing to deliver.
- You'd be out of the running.

68
00:03:05,268 --> 00:03:06,602
You were aiming high, huh?

69
00:03:06,603 --> 00:03:08,562
- No way.
- [Yoon Minseok] The card I took

70
00:03:08,563 --> 00:03:11,023
from the director
stated that his life depended on it.

71
00:03:11,024 --> 00:03:13,984
That's what he said
in his unsent text to Park Taeo.

72
00:03:13,985 --> 00:03:16,195
He said his life depended
on this campaign.

73
00:03:16,196 --> 00:03:19,865
Hear me out.
When trying to get players on board…

74
00:03:19,866 --> 00:03:21,909
Come on, you know how it goes.

75
00:03:21,910 --> 00:03:23,619
- "Help me out this once."
- [players laughing]

76
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:25,287
"Please. Just this once."

77
00:03:25,288 --> 00:03:27,624
"Hyunsoo, don't change teams.
Come back to Seoul."

78
00:03:28,208 --> 00:03:30,418
You say things like this.

79
00:03:30,419 --> 00:03:33,254
I had no idea,
but he's the chairman's son.

80
00:03:33,255 --> 00:03:34,547
As it turns out,

81
00:03:34,548 --> 00:03:37,925
<i>he was pushed out
of the race for succession.</i>

82
00:03:37,926 --> 00:03:39,427
THE CAMPAIGN WAS KEY
TO HIS SUCCESSION

83
00:03:39,428 --> 00:03:41,387
So, who would he resent the most?

84
00:03:41,388 --> 00:03:42,638
The late Park Taeo.

85
00:03:42,639 --> 00:03:44,682
He claims he said this and that

86
00:03:44,683 --> 00:03:47,476
to sweet-talk Taeo into collaborating,
but it's hardly likely.

87
00:03:47,477 --> 00:03:50,229
<i>He probably swore at him
and showed his true colors.</i>

88
00:03:50,230 --> 00:03:53,107
You might not have been so nice.

89
00:03:53,108 --> 00:03:55,443
"Think you're a big man?"

90
00:03:55,444 --> 00:03:57,778
- Yeah, I can see that.
- He might've threatened him.

91
00:03:57,779 --> 00:03:59,655
"You think you're still a big shot?"

92
00:03:59,656 --> 00:04:03,784
"What a joke. I'm the one
who made you a star."

93
00:04:03,785 --> 00:04:06,078
- You keep--
- "Your success has gone to your head."

94
00:04:06,079 --> 00:04:07,997
"How dare you act so big?"

95
00:04:07,998 --> 00:04:09,331
"You ungrateful jerk."

96
00:04:09,332 --> 00:04:11,000
Maybe you lost your temper.

97
00:04:11,001 --> 00:04:14,587
Which era are you living in?

98
00:04:14,588 --> 00:04:16,213
You can't do that in this day and age.

99
00:04:16,214 --> 00:04:17,506
I'm really sorry to interrupt,

100
00:04:17,507 --> 00:04:19,133
- but we don't have much time.
- Right.

101
00:04:19,134 --> 00:04:21,552
We need to check the CCTV,
so let's move on.

102
00:04:21,553 --> 00:04:22,928
- Good idea.
- First, Dohyun--

103
00:04:22,929 --> 00:04:25,973
- I took a card from Lee Hyunsoo.
- Okay.

104
00:04:25,974 --> 00:04:28,267
- You wrote in your training log…
- Okay.

105
00:04:28,268 --> 00:04:29,685
…"We had different starts."

106
00:04:29,686 --> 00:04:31,020
"If it wasn't for that ball…"

107
00:04:31,021 --> 00:04:32,104
- He felt inferior.
- Yeah.

108
00:04:32,105 --> 00:04:34,231
- There were a lot of entries like that.
- He was jealous.

109
00:04:34,232 --> 00:04:35,357
DID HE ENVY AND ADMIRE TAEO?

110
00:04:35,358 --> 00:04:37,860
[Kang Dohyun] There was a ball
at the crime scene.

111
00:04:37,861 --> 00:04:39,737
And the last
conclusive piece of evidence--

112
00:04:39,738 --> 00:04:41,322
- I'll check out the CCTV.
- Okay.

113
00:04:41,323 --> 00:04:42,990
Hang on.

114
00:04:42,991 --> 00:04:44,784
Dohyun talks too much.

115
00:04:44,785 --> 00:04:45,993
HAJUN HEADS TO THE CCTV ZONE AGAIN

116
00:04:45,994 --> 00:04:48,579
I also took a card from Lee Hyunsoo,

117
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:50,915
and it was also about his jealousy.

118
00:04:50,916 --> 00:04:53,292
- The king of jealousy.
- Yeah. The rundown is,

119
00:04:53,293 --> 00:04:54,710
the Major League teams

120
00:04:54,711 --> 00:04:57,713
were looking to sign Taeo first,

121
00:04:57,714 --> 00:04:59,673
but there was talk about signing Hyunsoo.

122
00:04:59,674 --> 00:05:01,175
- [exclaims]
- It was being discussed, but…

123
00:05:01,176 --> 00:05:02,719
Well, it's a really long story,

124
00:05:03,220 --> 00:05:05,513
but I had a son.

125
00:05:05,514 --> 00:05:07,014
A SON?

126
00:05:07,015 --> 00:05:08,766
- You had a son?
- [Yoon Minseok] Yes.

127
00:05:08,767 --> 00:05:10,184
- That was random.
- I had a son.

128
00:05:10,185 --> 00:05:11,644
- Suddenly?
- Dohyun knows.

129
00:05:11,645 --> 00:05:12,728
Of course, I know.

130
00:05:12,729 --> 00:05:14,980
- I had a son, but he died.
- Okay.

131
00:05:14,981 --> 00:05:16,106
Who killed him?

132
00:05:16,107 --> 00:05:17,650
[Yoon Minseok] I didn't know,

133
00:05:17,651 --> 00:05:19,026
but my son's name

134
00:05:19,027 --> 00:05:20,569
was Yoon Jaemin.

135
00:05:20,570 --> 00:05:22,321
But the Major League teams

136
00:05:22,322 --> 00:05:26,158
put their consideration
of Lee Hyunsoo on hold

137
00:05:26,159 --> 00:05:30,120
because of his connection
to my son's death.

138
00:05:30,121 --> 00:05:31,330
That's what the card said.

139
00:05:31,331 --> 00:05:33,958
I can explain exactly what happened.

140
00:05:33,959 --> 00:05:35,251
Can you?

141
00:05:35,252 --> 00:05:38,255
- What happened?
- You know I'm the king of jealousy.

142
00:05:38,922 --> 00:05:40,506
<i>When I was on the youth team,</i>

143
00:05:40,507 --> 00:05:43,634
<i>Park Taeo threw a ball at me
as a way of taunting me.</i>

144
00:05:43,635 --> 00:05:45,344
<i>Due to my burning jealousy,</i>

145
00:05:45,345 --> 00:05:47,388
<i>I snapped and whacked it back hard,</i>

146
00:05:47,389 --> 00:05:49,516
<i>but the ball flew in the direction</i>

147
00:05:50,100 --> 00:05:51,560
of Jaemin, the coach's son.

148
00:05:52,102 --> 00:05:53,185
SHOCK

149
00:05:53,186 --> 00:05:54,270
My son…

150
00:05:54,271 --> 00:05:56,063
- It was reckless intent.
- [Yoon Minseok] Right.

151
00:05:56,064 --> 00:05:57,940
- How awful.
- How could you take a life like that?

152
00:05:57,941 --> 00:05:59,316
[Lee Hyunsoo] <i>Following that incident,</i>

153
00:05:59,317 --> 00:06:02,361
<i>Park Taeo was cleared
of any connection to the tragedy.</i>

154
00:06:02,362 --> 00:06:04,947
- [Yoon Minseok] So you were the only--
- Yes, I took all the blame.

155
00:06:04,948 --> 00:06:08,576
Hold on. Then, you must
bear a grudge too, Coach.

156
00:06:08,577 --> 00:06:10,370
But I didn't know who was responsible.

157
00:06:10,954 --> 00:06:13,789
- How can you not know?
- He confessed that he was involved.

158
00:06:13,790 --> 00:06:15,541
- Here's why I didn't know.
- Okay.

159
00:06:15,542 --> 00:06:18,085
I was in complete despair at the time.

160
00:06:18,086 --> 00:06:22,131
Also, it was an incident involving
the Saints youth team,

161
00:06:22,132 --> 00:06:23,340
so I didn't press the issue.

162
00:06:23,341 --> 00:06:24,925
Of course, I was devastated.

163
00:06:24,926 --> 00:06:27,428
- You didn't dig into why your son died?
- [Kang Dohyun] Right?

164
00:06:27,429 --> 00:06:29,221
That's what it says here!

165
00:06:29,222 --> 00:06:30,598
That's what it says!

166
00:06:30,599 --> 00:06:32,016
- It makes no sense.
- Don't ask me!

167
00:06:32,017 --> 00:06:34,936
- I don't get it either!
- Your son died, yet you're here laughing.

168
00:06:36,104 --> 00:06:37,480
SOBBING

169
00:06:38,273 --> 00:06:39,523
Something's wrong with him.

170
00:06:39,524 --> 00:06:42,151
- My Jaemin!
- Is this normal?

171
00:06:42,152 --> 00:06:44,612
How can he sit here laughing
when his son died?

172
00:06:44,613 --> 00:06:46,740
You killed him? It was you?

173
00:06:47,449 --> 00:06:48,657
[Kim Doyun] <i>I don't understand</i>

174
00:06:48,658 --> 00:06:50,993
how the coach could be in the dark
about who killed his son

175
00:06:50,994 --> 00:06:53,787
<i>and even how he died.</i>

176
00:06:53,788 --> 00:06:56,957
I don't know.
It's only getting more confusing.

177
00:06:56,958 --> 00:07:01,003
I'm certain that Lee Hyunsoo
isn't the culprit in this case.

178
00:07:01,004 --> 00:07:03,130
As for the death of Yoon Jaemin,

179
00:07:03,131 --> 00:07:04,632
<i>it was an honest mistake.</i>

180
00:07:04,633 --> 00:07:06,133
<i>It was an unfortunate accident.</i>

181
00:07:06,134 --> 00:07:09,053
<i>But Park Taeo and Lee Hyunsoo
were responsible for killing my son.</i>

182
00:07:09,054 --> 00:07:10,512
I think that much is true.

183
00:07:10,513 --> 00:07:14,183
This bastard is the reason my son died,

184
00:07:14,184 --> 00:07:17,561
but I don't think he's connected
to this murder case.

185
00:07:17,562 --> 00:07:19,480
I brought this.

186
00:07:19,481 --> 00:07:20,564
HYUNSOO BROUGHT AN OBJECT CLUE

187
00:07:20,565 --> 00:07:22,608
- It's the fan club's ledger.
- Okay.

188
00:07:22,609 --> 00:07:26,362
- [Lee Hyunsoo] It shows Doyun knew the
- details and severity of Taeo's illness.

189
00:07:26,363 --> 00:07:28,489
We saw that earlier,
and this is further proof.

190
00:07:28,490 --> 00:07:33,202
<i>It's a ledger that focuses
only on Park Taeo.</i>

191
00:07:33,203 --> 00:07:35,204
LOOKING AROUND

192
00:07:35,205 --> 00:07:37,831
- Furthermore, on a computer…
- "Five thousand won."

193
00:07:37,832 --> 00:07:39,125
…he wrote a private post

194
00:07:39,918 --> 00:07:43,253
about wanting to get married.

195
00:07:43,254 --> 00:07:44,880
I knew it.

196
00:07:44,881 --> 00:07:45,882
They dated.

197
00:07:46,466 --> 00:07:47,467
You're right.

198
00:07:48,051 --> 00:07:50,261
- No, we didn't. This is…
- That's right.

199
00:07:51,096 --> 00:07:52,471
- What do you mean?
- The fan club.

200
00:07:52,472 --> 00:07:53,723
- The fan club--
- This guy…

201
00:07:54,307 --> 00:07:56,225
You may be behind the times,

202
00:07:56,226 --> 00:07:57,935
- but marriage is possible now.
- That's not it.

203
00:07:57,936 --> 00:08:00,396
- Surprisingly, it can happen.
- Who can get married?

204
00:08:00,397 --> 00:08:01,689
It's too far-fetched.

205
00:08:01,690 --> 00:08:03,899
- Same-sex marriage?
- [players] Yes.

206
00:08:03,900 --> 00:08:07,403
That's what it says on the card I took.
You did write a private post, right?

207
00:08:07,404 --> 00:08:09,655
- Who knew this was a possibility?
- This is why he became

208
00:08:09,656 --> 00:08:11,032
the president of a fan club.

209
00:08:12,117 --> 00:08:13,659
I'm into women.

210
00:08:13,660 --> 00:08:15,327
That's true in real life

211
00:08:15,328 --> 00:08:18,580
and for my character, Doyun.

212
00:08:18,581 --> 00:08:19,665
Why would he like men?

213
00:08:19,666 --> 00:08:23,085
<i>Of course, I respect people's preferences,
but I'm not personally inclined that way.</i>

214
00:08:23,086 --> 00:08:26,004
It's too much of a stretch, isn't it?

215
00:08:26,005 --> 00:08:29,675
I don't think it makes any sense
that I killed him because I loved him.

216
00:08:29,676 --> 00:08:31,343
[Lee Hyunsoo] It says here precisely…

217
00:08:31,344 --> 00:08:33,554
It says the post was written
by Kim Doyeon.

218
00:08:33,555 --> 00:08:34,638
The name…

219
00:08:34,639 --> 00:08:36,223
My name is spelled "yun."

220
00:08:36,224 --> 00:08:39,101
- What's up with that?
- It was written by a Kim Doyeon?

221
00:08:39,102 --> 00:08:40,477
- I saw that name…
- The name is--

222
00:08:40,478 --> 00:08:41,604
-…on a card.
- Mine's "yun."

223
00:08:42,230 --> 00:08:43,564
ROUND 1:
TAEO FANDOM ANALYSIS REPORT

224
00:08:43,565 --> 00:08:44,898
WRITTEN BY DOYEON, SENT TO HAJUN

225
00:08:44,899 --> 00:08:46,108
Who's Doyeon?

226
00:08:46,109 --> 00:08:48,569
This is strange. It says Doyeon.

227
00:08:48,570 --> 00:08:50,195
I saw that name earlier.

228
00:08:50,196 --> 00:08:52,282
Director Jo mentioned--

229
00:08:52,782 --> 00:08:54,158
HAJUN CHECKS THE CCTV AGAIN

230
00:08:54,159 --> 00:08:56,453
Let's take a look again. 31FE.

231
00:08:58,913 --> 00:09:02,041
Oh, he was shooting a documentary,

232
00:09:02,042 --> 00:09:04,461
so it was even more crucial
to keep his secrets under wraps.

233
00:09:05,045 --> 00:09:06,128
Got it.

234
00:09:06,129 --> 00:09:07,921
Either the coach or the manager.

235
00:09:07,922 --> 00:09:09,423
Then the prime suspects…

236
00:09:09,424 --> 00:09:10,758
Where have you been, Director?

237
00:09:10,759 --> 00:09:12,301
CURIOUS

238
00:09:12,302 --> 00:09:14,219
I just checked the CCTV.

239
00:09:14,220 --> 00:09:15,846
- I saw related footage.
- Okay.

240
00:09:15,847 --> 00:09:18,265
[Jo Hajun] It was a documentary
with an absurd title.

241
00:09:18,266 --> 00:09:19,349
What was it?

242
00:09:19,350 --> 00:09:21,811
<i>"The Legendary Kang Dohyun."</i>

243
00:09:22,395 --> 00:09:23,812
- Me?
- That's right.

244
00:09:23,813 --> 00:09:25,230
ME AGAIN?

245
00:09:25,231 --> 00:09:26,732
It's not me.

246
00:09:26,733 --> 00:09:28,817
You need to stop
barking up the wrong tree.

247
00:09:28,818 --> 00:09:30,069
Hear me out.

248
00:09:30,070 --> 00:09:33,739
He's not just a manager,
but "a legendary manager."

249
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:35,741
- He called himself that?
- [Kang Dohyun] Since I was young,

250
00:09:35,742 --> 00:09:38,577
- I dreamed of that.
- All right, I have something to share.

251
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:39,746
I found conclusive proof.

252
00:09:40,246 --> 00:09:42,039
"Kang Dohyun's kickback envelope."

253
00:09:42,040 --> 00:09:44,833
<i>It's a document about his kickbacks.</i>

254
00:09:44,834 --> 00:09:46,001
Look at the name.

255
00:09:46,002 --> 00:09:48,587
- It's the "legendary" Kang Dohyun.
- Okay.

256
00:09:48,588 --> 00:09:50,714
- He's a very messed-up guy.
- [Kang Dohyun] No, I'm not.

257
00:09:50,715 --> 00:09:52,466
- Jeez.
- What do you think of this?

258
00:09:52,467 --> 00:09:53,884
- No, listen.
- Can you explain it?

259
00:09:53,885 --> 00:09:56,011
The word "kickback" is a bit misleading.

260
00:09:56,012 --> 00:09:57,554
It's not a kickback.

261
00:09:57,555 --> 00:09:58,847
It's a sponsorship.

262
00:09:58,848 --> 00:09:59,932
It's management costs.

263
00:09:59,933 --> 00:10:03,811
Meeting reporters off the record
and things like that can be quite costly.

264
00:10:03,812 --> 00:10:08,232
In that case, did the hundred million won
that the director embezzled

265
00:10:08,233 --> 00:10:10,151
go into your pockets, Dohyun?

266
00:10:10,819 --> 00:10:13,737
- [Kim Doyun] Then it's all connected.
- Oh, you mean me?

267
00:10:13,738 --> 00:10:14,822
HAJUN EMBEZZLED MONEY?

268
00:10:14,823 --> 00:10:17,449
What are you talking about?
That's ridiculous.

269
00:10:17,450 --> 00:10:18,576
[sighs]

270
00:10:21,830 --> 00:10:23,330
Who are these people?

271
00:10:23,331 --> 00:10:25,040
ASSEMBLYMAN CHEOL MEETS PRIVATELY
WITH GEUMSEONG CHAIRMAN

272
00:10:25,041 --> 00:10:27,626
- There's someone called Cheol Ongsik.
- I saw that name too!

273
00:10:27,627 --> 00:10:28,752
[Kang Dohyun] Cheol Ongsik?

274
00:10:28,753 --> 00:10:29,962
He's just an assemblyman.

275
00:10:29,963 --> 00:10:31,797
- Why is he involved with you?
- An assemblyman?

276
00:10:31,798 --> 00:10:34,216
- He's a huge fan of our team.
- How is he connected?

277
00:10:34,217 --> 00:10:36,593
- What about it?
- That's why we're close.

278
00:10:36,594 --> 00:10:39,763
- He's one of our nation's representatives.
- Wait.

279
00:10:39,764 --> 00:10:42,975
If someone bribes a public official
with a hundred million won,

280
00:10:42,976 --> 00:10:45,686
- that's a big deal, right?
- It's huge. You go straight to jail.

281
00:10:45,687 --> 00:10:47,771
The manager should be
immediately arrested.

282
00:10:47,772 --> 00:10:49,356
You sent him a hundred million won first.

283
00:10:49,357 --> 00:10:51,316
I knew the assemblyman,
but I never bribed him.

284
00:10:51,317 --> 00:10:53,569
For goodness' sake. What are you on about?

285
00:10:53,570 --> 00:10:55,404
ROUND 3 CARD CLUES:
INTERNAL REPORT,

286
00:10:55,405 --> 00:10:57,239
TRAINING LOG, EMAIL,
FAN CLUB PRIVATE POST

287
00:10:57,240 --> 00:10:59,032
- Did you really not know?
- What?

288
00:10:59,033 --> 00:11:00,117
- Honestly?
- Know what?

289
00:11:00,118 --> 00:11:03,412
Just say you knew. I'll believe you more.

290
00:11:03,413 --> 00:11:06,123
- Oh, you mean who killed my son?
- Yeah.

291
00:11:06,124 --> 00:11:08,458
I'd be more convinced that you're innocent

292
00:11:08,459 --> 00:11:10,919
if you knew Park Taeo killed your son

293
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:13,297
because you kept that to yourself
for all these years.

294
00:11:13,298 --> 00:11:15,048
You were still his coach despite that.

295
00:11:15,049 --> 00:11:16,550
So I don't think it's noteworthy.

296
00:11:16,551 --> 00:11:19,845
But you not knowing
how your son died is a bit…

297
00:11:19,846 --> 00:11:22,306
I honestly didn't look into it
after his death.

298
00:11:22,307 --> 00:11:23,390
- Here's why.
- Okay.

299
00:11:23,391 --> 00:11:25,851
It happened on the Saints youth team,

300
00:11:25,852 --> 00:11:29,354
- and I didn't want to expose my own club.
- Mmm.

301
00:11:29,355 --> 00:11:31,565
Pressing the matter
wouldn't bring my son back,

302
00:11:31,566 --> 00:11:32,649
so I didn't dig deeper.

303
00:11:32,650 --> 00:11:35,944
My top suspect is still the manager.

304
00:11:35,945 --> 00:11:37,070
Look at this.

305
00:11:37,071 --> 00:11:40,365
Park Taeo was going to expose
the club's corruption, right?

306
00:11:40,366 --> 00:11:43,619
<i>I think it was connected
to the assemblyman and Geumseong Group.</i>

307
00:11:43,620 --> 00:11:45,746
- Can I ask you a question?
- Yeah.

308
00:11:45,747 --> 00:11:48,749
The hundred million won
on the secret ledger.

309
00:11:48,750 --> 00:11:49,833
Right, yes.

310
00:11:49,834 --> 00:11:51,543
You sent it to the manager, right?

311
00:11:51,544 --> 00:11:53,128
Honestly speaking,

312
00:11:53,129 --> 00:11:55,172
you could've sent him the money

313
00:11:55,173 --> 00:11:59,218
to bring in officials
like the assemblyman.

314
00:11:59,219 --> 00:12:01,678
Okay, I'll be honest, Hyunsoo.

315
00:12:01,679 --> 00:12:04,306
The parent company
run by my father, the chairman,

316
00:12:04,307 --> 00:12:05,849
ordered me to deliver the money,

317
00:12:05,850 --> 00:12:09,019
so I just did as I was told.

318
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:12,147
How much it was and what it was used for

319
00:12:12,148 --> 00:12:14,524
is beyond my knowledge.

320
00:12:14,525 --> 00:12:17,236
- My second suspect is the director.
- [Yoon Minseok] Right.

321
00:12:17,237 --> 00:12:21,615
Do you remember how I kept asking him
if he recalled the cake?

322
00:12:21,616 --> 00:12:23,825
I have a question for you.

323
00:12:23,826 --> 00:12:26,411
What do you think about the cake?

324
00:12:26,412 --> 00:12:28,497
- The cake?
- Yes. What are your thoughts on it?

325
00:12:28,498 --> 00:12:31,708
It was a congratulatory party,

326
00:12:31,709 --> 00:12:33,961
so it's only natural
there was champagne and a cake.

327
00:12:33,962 --> 00:12:36,755
The director got me to deliver that cake.

328
00:12:36,756 --> 00:12:38,048
THE FAN CLUB PRESIDENT
DELIVERED THE CAKE?

329
00:12:38,049 --> 00:12:40,093
He made me deliver the cake.

330
00:12:40,593 --> 00:12:42,010
But this is a secret

331
00:12:42,011 --> 00:12:44,304
because I plan to confront him
about it at the discussion table.

332
00:12:44,305 --> 00:12:47,349
Here's what I'm wondering.
We don't know the exact cause of death.

333
00:12:47,350 --> 00:12:48,725
He was hit by a bat,

334
00:12:48,726 --> 00:12:50,602
but he could've been killed
some other way first

335
00:12:50,603 --> 00:12:52,354
and then hit with the bat afterward

336
00:12:52,355 --> 00:12:55,440
- to make it seem like the murder weapon.
- Right.

337
00:12:55,441 --> 00:12:57,026
And that's why the culprit used my bat.

338
00:12:57,610 --> 00:12:59,153
You really never hit him?

339
00:12:59,737 --> 00:13:01,446
Even if you didn't kill him,

340
00:13:01,447 --> 00:13:03,198
you never even smacked his bum?

341
00:13:03,199 --> 00:13:04,449
- No, I didn't.
- Really?

342
00:13:04,450 --> 00:13:06,285
- You're sure?
- I never hit him.

343
00:13:06,286 --> 00:13:09,329
It's almost impossible to kill
a sturdy baseball player with a bat

344
00:13:09,330 --> 00:13:12,416
without him fighting back.

345
00:13:12,417 --> 00:13:17,004
<i>But if someone got a cake
to make it easier to kill him,</i>

346
00:13:17,005 --> 00:13:19,881
<i>it must be either the director
or the fan club president.</i>

347
00:13:19,882 --> 00:13:21,258
But I'm not sure which one.

348
00:13:21,259 --> 00:13:22,968
It's too hard to tell.

349
00:13:22,969 --> 00:13:25,721
[host] <i>Here is the fourth shared clue.</i>

350
00:13:25,722 --> 00:13:28,223
- The fan club president's insulin.
- [Kang Dohyun] Right.

351
00:13:28,224 --> 00:13:29,308
For managing his glucose.

352
00:13:29,309 --> 00:13:30,852
- This.
- But it's not been used.

353
00:13:31,436 --> 00:13:33,687
- It's new.
- It's not been used?

354
00:13:33,688 --> 00:13:36,273
[Yoon Minseok] <i>I think someone tossed it
before it could be used.</i>

355
00:13:36,274 --> 00:13:37,357
SOMEONE THREW IT AWAY?

356
00:13:37,358 --> 00:13:40,944
I'll take a card from the coach,
who's got more secrets than I thought.

357
00:13:40,945 --> 00:13:44,698
I'll take the manager's last card
to seal the case against him.

358
00:13:44,699 --> 00:13:47,159
Are you that upset with me?

359
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:49,661
Sorry. It's not because I doubt you.

360
00:13:49,662 --> 00:13:51,246
- You should just take mine…
- [Kang Dohyun] Sure.

361
00:13:51,247 --> 00:13:52,789
…since it's my last one.

362
00:13:52,790 --> 00:13:55,500
Since this insulin
is pretty strong evidence…

363
00:13:55,501 --> 00:13:57,294
But I also need to look into the director.

364
00:13:57,295 --> 00:13:58,754
These are our last card clues, right?

365
00:13:58,755 --> 00:14:00,547
COLLECTING OBJECT CLUES

366
00:14:00,548 --> 00:14:02,507
- We searched these.
- I got the one from locker one.

367
00:14:02,508 --> 00:14:03,676
We didn't check locker six.

368
00:14:06,304 --> 00:14:07,305
Found it.

369
00:14:08,306 --> 00:14:11,016
I have a record in my hand.

370
00:14:11,017 --> 00:14:12,768
It seems the fan club president

371
00:14:12,769 --> 00:14:14,728
has a VIP entry pass.

372
00:14:14,729 --> 00:14:16,396
We both got one.

373
00:14:16,397 --> 00:14:19,191
How can a fan club president
have a VIP pass?

374
00:14:19,192 --> 00:14:23,236
The record shows an entry at 11 p.m.
But why did you enter again at midnight?

375
00:14:23,237 --> 00:14:25,864
- I didn't go back in at midnight.
- What? Midnight?

376
00:14:25,865 --> 00:14:27,991
Did you cross paths with Park Taeo?

377
00:14:27,992 --> 00:14:29,618
I met him at 11:05 p.m.

378
00:14:29,619 --> 00:14:31,745
- You met him at 11:05 p.m.?
- Yes.

379
00:14:31,746 --> 00:14:33,080
You checked in with your pass?

380
00:14:33,081 --> 00:14:35,332
No, 11:05… I'll explain exactly.

381
00:14:35,333 --> 00:14:38,252
- I met the director at 10:50 p.m.…
- Okay.

382
00:14:39,212 --> 00:14:41,798
…and he told me to deliver
the cake to the locker room.

383
00:14:42,548 --> 00:14:44,382
That's right. It was around that time.

384
00:14:44,383 --> 00:14:46,343
But why didn't you
disclose that right away?

385
00:14:46,344 --> 00:14:48,303
You didn't mention the cake.

386
00:14:48,304 --> 00:14:50,764
The cake isn't very important.

387
00:14:50,765 --> 00:14:53,433
- Anyway--
- It keeps coming up as evidence.

388
00:14:53,434 --> 00:14:55,560
- [Yoon Minseok] So you delivered the cake?
- I delivered it.

389
00:14:55,561 --> 00:14:57,896
- What time?
- [Kim Doyun] At 11:05 p.m.

390
00:14:57,897 --> 00:15:00,774
- 11:05 p.m.?
- I delivered the cake at 11:05 p.m.

391
00:15:00,775 --> 00:15:02,025
and left five minutes later.

392
00:15:02,026 --> 00:15:03,485
I was only there for five minutes.

393
00:15:03,486 --> 00:15:04,779
But on my way out,

394
00:15:06,405 --> 00:15:07,782
I saw Lee Hyunsoo.

395
00:15:08,282 --> 00:15:10,784
DOYUN AND HYUNSOO CROSSED PATHS
OUTSIDE THE LOCKERS

396
00:15:10,785 --> 00:15:12,911
- We crossed paths, right?
- Yeah, we did.

397
00:15:12,912 --> 00:15:14,579
- Taeo was alive until then.
- Yes.

398
00:15:14,580 --> 00:15:17,582
- Our Taeo was still alive until then.
- You didn't go back in at midnight?

399
00:15:17,583 --> 00:15:18,917
"Our Taeo"?

400
00:15:18,918 --> 00:15:21,002
- That's very suspicious.
- He's our player.

401
00:15:21,003 --> 00:15:25,549
Who has the most information
out of all of us?

402
00:15:25,550 --> 00:15:28,510
<i>When the ace player
went into hypoglycemic shock,</i>

403
00:15:28,511 --> 00:15:30,929
<i>I think the only person
who knew his condition inside out</i>

404
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:32,722
<i>was the fan club president,
so he's the top suspect.</i>

405
00:15:32,723 --> 00:15:35,518
But we need to investigate
to see if that's true.

406
00:15:36,435 --> 00:15:39,105
If this confirms it,
then it's case closed.

407
00:15:40,731 --> 00:15:41,732
Who's that?

408
00:15:45,736 --> 00:15:47,238
It's CCTV footage of the stadium.

409
00:15:49,574 --> 00:15:53,160
He was about to expose something to do
with the assemblyman.

410
00:15:53,161 --> 00:15:55,078
- Oh, you're right.
- That's not it.

411
00:15:55,079 --> 00:15:58,248
- I just checked the CCTV.
- Yes?

412
00:15:58,249 --> 00:16:00,250
What time did you say
you went home earlier?

413
00:16:00,251 --> 00:16:02,002
- When did you leave the stadium?
- 11 p.m.

414
00:16:02,003 --> 00:16:03,837
- No, at 11:05 p.m.…
- Yes?

415
00:16:03,838 --> 00:16:05,505
-…I delivered the cake and ran into you.
- Yeah.

416
00:16:05,506 --> 00:16:07,341
And when I left,

417
00:16:07,842 --> 00:16:10,802
- it was around midnight.
- Midnight?

418
00:16:10,803 --> 00:16:12,262
- Can I check quickly?
- But…

419
00:16:12,263 --> 00:16:13,972
- Hold on.
- [Lee Hyunsoo] But the CCTV footage showed

420
00:16:13,973 --> 00:16:15,557
you were there at 2:17 a.m.,

421
00:16:15,558 --> 00:16:17,642
- looking right at the camera.
- [players exclaim]

422
00:16:17,643 --> 00:16:18,852
- Wait a minute.
- I've got chills.

423
00:16:18,853 --> 00:16:20,896
- It was 2 a.m.?
- It was 2:17 a.m.

424
00:16:20,897 --> 00:16:23,274
- I've got chills.
- The culprit reappeared at the scene.

425
00:16:23,816 --> 00:16:26,318
HYUNSOO MISREAD 12:02 A.M.
AS 02:02 A.M.

426
00:16:26,319 --> 00:16:27,485
Your alibi is totally…

427
00:16:27,486 --> 00:16:28,612
- You lunatic!
- [Jo Hajun] Wait.

428
00:16:28,613 --> 00:16:29,696
- It was 12:17 a.m.
- Wait.

429
00:16:29,697 --> 00:16:31,073
You little!

430
00:16:31,657 --> 00:16:33,241
Why did you hit me?

431
00:16:33,242 --> 00:16:34,451
HE GOT SLAPPED

432
00:16:34,452 --> 00:16:36,328
I mean…

433
00:16:36,329 --> 00:16:37,872
He got physical!

434
00:16:38,581 --> 00:16:39,706
[Kim Doyun] Why did you do that?

435
00:16:39,707 --> 00:16:40,958
Why did you hit me?

436
00:16:41,542 --> 00:16:44,127
- I'm sorry.
- What the heck?

437
00:16:44,128 --> 00:16:45,754
I got riled up.

438
00:16:45,755 --> 00:16:47,756
This must be how you killed Park Taeo!

439
00:16:47,757 --> 00:16:49,591
He beat him to death like this.

440
00:16:49,592 --> 00:16:51,134
It was forceful enough to kill someone.

441
00:16:51,135 --> 00:16:52,386
That's how he killed him.

442
00:16:52,887 --> 00:16:54,429
- Hold on.
- I'm sorry.

443
00:16:54,430 --> 00:16:56,223
Hang on.

444
00:16:56,224 --> 00:16:58,308
That's not right. I went back at 2 a.m.?

445
00:16:58,309 --> 00:16:59,935
It was 12:07 a.m.

446
00:16:59,936 --> 00:17:02,896
Yeah, it was close to midnight.
It was just past it.

447
00:17:02,897 --> 00:17:03,980
ROUND 4 CARD CLUES

448
00:17:03,981 --> 00:17:05,482
NEWS ARTICLE, COACH'S ACCESS
PASS, STADIUM ACCESS RECORD,

449
00:17:05,483 --> 00:17:06,566
DRIVER'S LICENSE,
DOCUMENTARY CONTRACT

450
00:17:06,567 --> 00:17:08,526
[host] <i>Round 4 is over.</i>

451
00:17:08,527 --> 00:17:10,112
<i>It is time for the private conversations.</i>

452
00:17:10,905 --> 00:17:13,198
You've been through a lot, Director.

453
00:17:13,199 --> 00:17:14,408
After delivering the cake,

454
00:17:14,992 --> 00:17:18,119
why did you linger around afterward?

455
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:19,621
When did I linger?

456
00:17:19,622 --> 00:17:22,666
Did you really not see Park Taeo again
after delivering the cake?

457
00:17:22,667 --> 00:17:23,959
Not after I delivered the cake.

458
00:17:23,960 --> 00:17:26,670
Between 11 p.m. and midnight,
the estimated time of the crime,

459
00:17:26,671 --> 00:17:30,423
- the only one who met Park Taeo for sure…
- That's right.

460
00:17:30,424 --> 00:17:32,467
-…the only one with an alibi is…
- Yeah, it's me.

461
00:17:32,468 --> 00:17:33,718
- It's you.
- Yeah.

462
00:17:33,719 --> 00:17:36,763
But I bumped into Lee Hyunsoo
on my way out,

463
00:17:36,764 --> 00:17:39,182
and he went in after me.

464
00:17:39,183 --> 00:17:42,811
The players were celebrating together,
so it makes sense he was there.

465
00:17:42,812 --> 00:17:44,521
My point is that Park Taeo was alive.

466
00:17:44,522 --> 00:17:46,481
I just delivered the cake then left.

467
00:17:46,482 --> 00:17:48,775
He was either still alive

468
00:17:48,776 --> 00:17:50,527
or he was already dead,

469
00:17:50,528 --> 00:17:52,946
but Lee Hyunsoo is playing dumb.

470
00:17:52,947 --> 00:17:56,157
No. You can't accuse me like this.

471
00:17:56,158 --> 00:17:57,993
- Why not?
- Because it was a bit suspicious

472
00:17:57,994 --> 00:18:00,412
- that you got me to deliver the cake.
- Right.

473
00:18:00,413 --> 00:18:02,789
- The cake was the centerpiece.
- Yeah.

474
00:18:02,790 --> 00:18:05,166
- It looked like the whole thing was eaten.
- It was.

475
00:18:05,167 --> 00:18:07,503
So I wondered
if it had been laced with pills.

476
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:09,588
You think I put something in it?

477
00:18:09,589 --> 00:18:13,758
It'd make sense if he fainted
due to low blood sugar.

478
00:18:13,759 --> 00:18:15,510
- But I didn't suspect you.
- Right.

479
00:18:15,511 --> 00:18:17,596
- But if you suspect me like this…
- No, no.

480
00:18:17,597 --> 00:18:19,932
- No, listen.
- That's a bit upsetting.

481
00:18:20,850 --> 00:18:22,392
- Look.
- You get me, right?

482
00:18:22,393 --> 00:18:25,020
Then let me just ask you
one last question.

483
00:18:25,021 --> 00:18:27,689
Do you know when Park Taeo

484
00:18:27,690 --> 00:18:29,733
needed to take medication or get injected?

485
00:18:29,734 --> 00:18:32,569
Do you know his treatment schedule?

486
00:18:32,570 --> 00:18:34,863
I don't know the exact times
he needed his injection.

487
00:18:34,864 --> 00:18:36,615
I just know that he needed injections.

488
00:18:36,616 --> 00:18:38,158
But you don't know the time frame?

489
00:18:38,159 --> 00:18:39,368
Time frame?

490
00:18:39,994 --> 00:18:41,202
- Me?
- Yeah.

491
00:18:41,203 --> 00:18:42,371
No, I don't.

492
00:18:45,082 --> 00:18:47,334
We're looking for the killer,

493
00:18:47,335 --> 00:18:51,463
so we need proof that they used
the insulin shot somehow.

494
00:18:51,464 --> 00:18:53,298
- We can connect it to the director's cake…
- Yeah.

495
00:18:53,299 --> 00:18:57,802
…and the fan club president said
he went around with the cake.

496
00:18:57,803 --> 00:19:00,513
Do we think there's a twist or…

497
00:19:00,514 --> 00:19:02,349
- Or do we think by the book?
- Exactly.

498
00:19:02,350 --> 00:19:05,895
We're focusing too much
on just the director.

499
00:19:06,979 --> 00:19:08,396
This is so hard.

500
00:19:08,397 --> 00:19:10,774
[host] <i>Here is the final shared clue.</i>

501
00:19:10,775 --> 00:19:11,858
[Lee Hyunsoo] At last.

502
00:19:11,859 --> 00:19:13,903
- If only we got it sooner.
- [Jo Hajun] It's the conclusive proof.

503
00:19:14,403 --> 00:19:17,405
"The immediate cause of death
was intracranial hemorrhage

504
00:19:17,406 --> 00:19:19,282
and brain injury
due to blunt head trauma."

505
00:19:19,283 --> 00:19:20,408
"The antecedent cause

506
00:19:20,409 --> 00:19:23,328
was altered consciousness
due to acute hypoglycemic shock."

507
00:19:23,329 --> 00:19:25,872
"The underlying cause
was metabolic abnormality due to fasting,

508
00:19:25,873 --> 00:19:28,083
dehydration,
and excessive alcohol consumption."

509
00:19:28,084 --> 00:19:30,001
There are three causes of death?

510
00:19:30,002 --> 00:19:32,754
- The immediate cause points to the killer.
- Right.

511
00:19:32,755 --> 00:19:36,091
I think the blunt trauma
was caused by the bat.

512
00:19:36,092 --> 00:19:37,634
- He hit him with the bat first.
- Yeah.

513
00:19:37,635 --> 00:19:40,762
Park Taeo didn't take medication
for hypoglycemic shock before that?

514
00:19:40,763 --> 00:19:42,764
Who made the cake again?

515
00:19:42,765 --> 00:19:44,891
- It was made by our director.
- No, hold on.

516
00:19:44,892 --> 00:19:46,185
I didn't make the cake.

517
00:19:46,811 --> 00:19:48,978
- Yes, you did.
- I delivered it.

518
00:19:48,979 --> 00:19:51,189
I'm a director, not a baker.

519
00:19:51,190 --> 00:19:52,691
- Okay, you delivered it.
- I did.

520
00:19:52,692 --> 00:19:53,942
Where did you buy it from?

521
00:19:53,943 --> 00:19:56,361
I got a subordinate
to go and buy the cake.

522
00:19:56,362 --> 00:19:57,696
[Yoon Minseok] Here's the conclusion.

523
00:19:57,697 --> 00:20:02,200
If you have low blood sugar,
eating cake raises it back to normal.

524
00:20:02,201 --> 00:20:03,284
- Right?
- Usually, yes.

525
00:20:03,285 --> 00:20:04,869
But to prevent that,

526
00:20:04,870 --> 00:20:06,788
instead of using sugar,

527
00:20:06,789 --> 00:20:09,040
the culprit may have used
a substitute like Stevia.

528
00:20:09,041 --> 00:20:11,418
Normally, eating the cake
should lead to a blood sugar spike,

529
00:20:11,419 --> 00:20:13,670
but because it didn't,
it led to hypoglycemic shock.

530
00:20:13,671 --> 00:20:16,464
Or the culprit might've
masked the taste of alcohol

531
00:20:16,465 --> 00:20:20,552
- so he drank it without knowing.
- Could be why he drank excessively.

532
00:20:20,553 --> 00:20:22,762
This was planned
by the person who made the cake.

533
00:20:22,763 --> 00:20:26,683
But if it's someone who could
bake a cake with all that in mind,

534
00:20:26,684 --> 00:20:29,477
the only one who fits the bill
is the fan club president.

535
00:20:29,478 --> 00:20:32,439
- He's the only one with that knowledge.
- But it was given to him

536
00:20:32,440 --> 00:20:33,606
- by the director.
- That's not it.

537
00:20:33,607 --> 00:20:35,400
He just passed on the cake.

538
00:20:35,401 --> 00:20:36,860
- You think he switched the cakes?
- Yeah.

539
00:20:36,861 --> 00:20:38,987
<i>-He swapped it.
- Wait.</i>

540
00:20:38,988 --> 00:20:40,697
- No, I didn't.
- The cake didn't kill him.

541
00:20:40,698 --> 00:20:43,158
We know now that the cake didn't kill him.

542
00:20:43,159 --> 00:20:45,785
So I think that makes
the cake more important

543
00:20:45,786 --> 00:20:47,120
because after it was delivered,

544
00:20:47,121 --> 00:20:49,497
the VIP pass was used
one more time, right?

545
00:20:49,498 --> 00:20:53,585
So he knew that the cake
would make Park Taeo faint,

546
00:20:53,586 --> 00:20:56,963
and he went back to finish him off
by using the VIP card for access.

547
00:20:56,964 --> 00:20:59,758
To add to what he just said,

548
00:20:59,759 --> 00:21:01,676
Kim Doyun, the fan club president,

549
00:21:01,677 --> 00:21:04,554
knew that between 11 p.m. and 11:30 p.m.,

550
00:21:04,555 --> 00:21:09,851
Park Taeo had to take the insulin shot
or it could badly affect his health.

551
00:21:09,852 --> 00:21:11,978
- He knew that from the start.
- Yeah.

552
00:21:11,979 --> 00:21:14,022
I knew that he needed
to manage his glucose levels.

553
00:21:14,023 --> 00:21:16,858
Here's the thing. It's common knowledge
among the fan club members.

554
00:21:16,859 --> 00:21:19,360
When I asked the fan club president,

555
00:21:19,361 --> 00:21:20,904
he said he didn't know

556
00:21:20,905 --> 00:21:23,990
<i>the exact time frame,
but he changed his story.</i>

557
00:21:23,991 --> 00:21:30,038
I think Kim Doyun
had more than enough time to kill Taeo.

558
00:21:30,039 --> 00:21:31,873
- I'm going to check the CCTV.
- Sure.

559
00:21:31,874 --> 00:21:35,251
There will probably be CCTV footage of me.

560
00:21:35,252 --> 00:21:36,836
I'm just giving you a heads up.

561
00:21:36,837 --> 00:21:38,379
- All of a sudden?
- Hear me out.

562
00:21:38,380 --> 00:21:40,632
- He's laying the groundwork.
- Here's why I'm telling you.

563
00:21:40,633 --> 00:21:43,218
I shouldn't say this,
but I really want to catch the culprit.

564
00:21:43,219 --> 00:21:45,512
I actually went into the locker room.

565
00:21:45,513 --> 00:21:46,679
What?

566
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:49,183
"D, S, H, E."

567
00:21:49,725 --> 00:21:53,020
D, S, H, E.

568
00:21:54,188 --> 00:21:55,272
What's this?

569
00:21:55,773 --> 00:21:57,983
DASHCAM FOOTAGE?

570
00:22:10,788 --> 00:22:13,540
SD CARD MISSING

571
00:22:13,541 --> 00:22:15,917
To be honest, I planned to kill Park Taeo.

572
00:22:15,918 --> 00:22:17,502
- [gasps]
- [Yoon Minseok] But when I entered,

573
00:22:17,503 --> 00:22:19,337
I found that he was

574
00:22:19,338 --> 00:22:20,881
already dead.

575
00:22:21,507 --> 00:22:24,717
I'm bringing this up now
because it might help solve the case.

576
00:22:24,718 --> 00:22:26,427
I'm not supposed to reveal this.

577
00:22:26,428 --> 00:22:28,429
- Right.
- I'm not meant to reveal it,

578
00:22:28,430 --> 00:22:31,641
but if I keep it to myself,
you'll think I'm the culprit,

579
00:22:31,642 --> 00:22:33,476
so I'm telling you
to save you the confusion.

580
00:22:33,477 --> 00:22:35,353
<i>I actually went into the locker room,</i>

581
00:22:35,354 --> 00:22:39,065
<i>and I even had a bat ready to kill Taeo,
but he was already dead.</i>

582
00:22:39,066 --> 00:22:40,400
Why didn't I report it?

583
00:22:40,401 --> 00:22:44,821
I suspected that he was responsible
for my son's death,

584
00:22:44,822 --> 00:22:46,281
so I thought he was justly punished.

585
00:22:46,282 --> 00:22:48,867
He got what he deserved,
so I didn't report it.

586
00:22:48,868 --> 00:22:50,201
- That's cold.
- But I didn't kill him.

587
00:22:50,202 --> 00:22:51,744
I think the cake was used

588
00:22:51,745 --> 00:22:54,372
by the director or the fan club president

589
00:22:54,373 --> 00:22:57,166
just to knock him out,
but they didn't kill him.

590
00:22:57,167 --> 00:22:58,585
It was someone else.

591
00:22:58,586 --> 00:23:01,129
We're looking for the person
who caused the blunt head trauma.

592
00:23:01,130 --> 00:23:05,091
I was suspicious of the director
and the fan club president.

593
00:23:05,092 --> 00:23:06,175
- Suddenly?
- Just like me,

594
00:23:06,176 --> 00:23:08,344
you both intended to kill him,

595
00:23:08,345 --> 00:23:11,264
- but someone else actually did it.
- You're getting out of it like this?

596
00:23:11,265 --> 00:23:14,350
It's not very believable.
Coach Yoon is a very smart man.

597
00:23:14,351 --> 00:23:15,436
He's very sly.

598
00:23:15,936 --> 00:23:18,980
<i>His son died,
so it was a father's revenge.</i>

599
00:23:18,981 --> 00:23:22,191
<i>I somewhat understand it,
but he shouldn't have done that.</i>

600
00:23:22,192 --> 00:23:25,612
I think it was a very calculated excuse.

601
00:23:25,613 --> 00:23:27,864
Thinking about it now,

602
00:23:27,865 --> 00:23:30,326
he might not have been dead
when I saw him.

603
00:23:31,035 --> 00:23:32,702
You saw him dead?

604
00:23:32,703 --> 00:23:35,371
- While you were checking out the CCTV--
- Yeah, I missed it.

605
00:23:35,372 --> 00:23:36,623
- When I saw him--
- What time?

606
00:23:36,624 --> 00:23:38,499
It was around 11:30 p.m.

607
00:23:38,500 --> 00:23:40,585
It was sometime
between 11 p.m. and 12 a.m.

608
00:23:40,586 --> 00:23:42,003
- I went there to kill him.
- Okay.

609
00:23:42,004 --> 00:23:43,546
- But--
- You planned to kill him?

610
00:23:43,547 --> 00:23:44,631
That's what he said.

611
00:23:44,632 --> 00:23:46,382
I'm not meant to reveal that,
so why did I?

612
00:23:46,383 --> 00:23:49,385
Why would I share such crucial evidence?
Because I'm not guilty.

613
00:23:49,386 --> 00:23:53,806
I was going to kill him,
so I headed over with my bat,

614
00:23:53,807 --> 00:23:55,475
but he was already unconscious.

615
00:23:55,476 --> 00:23:58,937
But that was just the result
of his primary and secondary injuries.

616
00:23:58,938 --> 00:24:02,357
I found him unconscious
due to hypoglycemic shock,

617
00:24:02,358 --> 00:24:05,610
and whoever went in after I left
might be the one who killed him.

618
00:24:05,611 --> 00:24:06,694
You didn't hit him?

619
00:24:06,695 --> 00:24:08,112
No, I didn't.

620
00:24:08,113 --> 00:24:11,616
- And you didn't feed him anything?
- No, I never saw the cake before today.

621
00:24:11,617 --> 00:24:13,826
Let me share what I found.

622
00:24:13,827 --> 00:24:16,621
Do you like driving, Coach Yoon?

623
00:24:16,622 --> 00:24:17,705
- Driving?
- Yes.

624
00:24:17,706 --> 00:24:18,790
I don't drive.

625
00:24:18,791 --> 00:24:20,208
- What?
- I don't drive.

626
00:24:20,209 --> 00:24:21,751
- You're unlicensed?
- You have no license?

627
00:24:21,752 --> 00:24:23,461
I do, but I don't drive.

628
00:24:23,462 --> 00:24:25,296
Why not if you have a license?

629
00:24:25,297 --> 00:24:27,173
I'll explain.

630
00:24:27,174 --> 00:24:28,883
The statute of limitations has expired

631
00:24:28,884 --> 00:24:30,843
for his hit-and-run crime.

632
00:24:30,844 --> 00:24:32,470
The expiry time and date

633
00:24:32,471 --> 00:24:35,723
were 11 p.m. on October 31, 2025.

634
00:24:35,724 --> 00:24:37,725
Remember the dates that were crossed out?

635
00:24:37,726 --> 00:24:39,310
<i>It was the expiry date.</i>

636
00:24:39,311 --> 00:24:41,729
<i>-Why did you count down until that day?</i>
- [Yoon Minseok] <i>Hear me out.</i>

637
00:24:41,730 --> 00:24:43,606
It's not very relevant to this case.

638
00:24:43,607 --> 00:24:46,401
I didn't want to waste time
on something pointless.

639
00:24:46,402 --> 00:24:47,860
- But I'm curious.
- I'll explain.

640
00:24:47,861 --> 00:24:51,489
Park Taeo killed my son many years ago.

641
00:24:51,490 --> 00:24:53,116
- Yes.
- It was involuntary manslaughter.

642
00:24:53,117 --> 00:24:57,161
Manager Kang Dohyun suggested
we get a drink, so I had a few drinks.

643
00:24:57,162 --> 00:24:58,914
<i>-I have no memory of the event…
- Okay.</i>

644
00:24:59,540 --> 00:25:00,708
<i>…but I hit someone while driving.</i>

645
00:25:01,417 --> 00:25:02,542
I killed someone.

646
00:25:02,543 --> 00:25:03,751
- Due to drink driving?
- Yes.

647
00:25:03,752 --> 00:25:06,004
- Why didn't you tell us that?
- It wasn't necessary.

648
00:25:06,005 --> 00:25:07,547
It's irrelevant to this case.

649
00:25:07,548 --> 00:25:08,631
I didn't bring it up

650
00:25:08,632 --> 00:25:11,801
- because it's not related to Taeo's death.
- It is relevant.

651
00:25:11,802 --> 00:25:13,094
He found out your secret.

652
00:25:13,095 --> 00:25:14,262
DID TAEO WITNESS
THE HIT-AND-RUN?

653
00:25:14,263 --> 00:25:16,764
He questioned you about it,
so you got angry

654
00:25:16,765 --> 00:25:19,434
because you were waiting
for the statute of limitations to expire.

655
00:25:19,435 --> 00:25:21,853
You were just one day away from freedom.

656
00:25:21,854 --> 00:25:22,937
That wasn't in my guide.

657
00:25:22,938 --> 00:25:24,355
- Is that why--
- What on earth?

658
00:25:24,356 --> 00:25:27,191
Is that why you resolved
to kill him right away?

659
00:25:27,192 --> 00:25:29,736
As I told you earlier,
I was planning to kill him.

660
00:25:29,737 --> 00:25:30,987
I even had a bat ready.

661
00:25:30,988 --> 00:25:32,489
But he was already knocked out.

662
00:25:33,073 --> 00:25:36,993
- Taeo was attacked in the locker room.
- What he's saying is…

663
00:25:36,994 --> 00:25:38,703
- It's conclusive.
- He had two sets of injuries.

664
00:25:38,704 --> 00:25:40,913
But he was killed by a third injury.

665
00:25:40,914 --> 00:25:42,206
Here's what I think.

666
00:25:42,207 --> 00:25:44,459
<i>The large pool of blood</i>

667
00:25:44,460 --> 00:25:46,669
- formed while he was still alive, right?
- Yeah.

668
00:25:46,670 --> 00:25:49,714
That's when I walked in
and saw him unconscious.

669
00:25:49,715 --> 00:25:51,758
I thought he was dead,
so I turned around and left.

670
00:25:51,759 --> 00:25:52,967
But I think he died after that.

671
00:25:52,968 --> 00:25:56,429
I honestly think someone else
delivered the fatal blow.

672
00:25:56,430 --> 00:25:58,431
From a logical standpoint,

673
00:25:58,432 --> 00:26:01,934
one person walked in on him alive,
and another found him dead.

674
00:26:01,935 --> 00:26:03,227
One of them must be the killer.

675
00:26:03,228 --> 00:26:06,106
<i>It must be Hyunsoo or the coach,
who went in after me.</i>

676
00:26:06,899 --> 00:26:09,317
- Doyun.
- Yes?

677
00:26:09,318 --> 00:26:12,612
Did you know about Park Taeo's girlfriend?

678
00:26:12,613 --> 00:26:14,864
- Park Taeo's girlfriend? Yes, I knew.
- Yes.

679
00:26:14,865 --> 00:26:16,157
- You knew?
- Yes.

680
00:26:16,158 --> 00:26:17,658
- What?
- Did that upset you?

681
00:26:17,659 --> 00:26:19,202
- Taeo's girlfriend?
- His girlfriend…

682
00:26:19,203 --> 00:26:20,453
What are you talking about?

683
00:26:20,454 --> 00:26:21,663
He cheated.

684
00:26:22,539 --> 00:26:24,291
You liked Park Taeo, didn't you?

685
00:26:25,292 --> 00:26:26,668
[laughter]

686
00:26:27,377 --> 00:26:28,920
- This is…
- Listen.

687
00:26:28,921 --> 00:26:30,296
[Kim Doyun] I'm sorry, but…

688
00:26:30,297 --> 00:26:31,798
Don't hit me. Hear me out.

689
00:26:31,799 --> 00:26:33,257
Why would I hit you for having a crush?

690
00:26:33,258 --> 00:26:34,425
Here's the thing.

691
00:26:34,426 --> 00:26:37,346
- Granted, in this roleplay…
- Am I right?

692
00:26:37,930 --> 00:26:39,555
…my character's a bit random.

693
00:26:39,556 --> 00:26:40,765
- That said…
- Yes?

694
00:26:40,766 --> 00:26:42,809
…I don't think they would

695
00:26:42,810 --> 00:26:44,645
move the story in that direction.

696
00:26:45,354 --> 00:26:49,273
I can acknowledge everything else,
but I'm the only one without a motive.

697
00:26:49,274 --> 00:26:51,859
You felt the most betrayed
since he didn't love you back.

698
00:26:51,860 --> 00:26:54,654
Some fans think players should
only focus on their career

699
00:26:54,655 --> 00:26:57,281
instead of being distracted
by dating and marriage.

700
00:26:57,282 --> 00:26:59,743
Then was his girlfriend
your younger sister?

701
00:27:00,327 --> 00:27:01,828
WAS TAEO'S GIRLFRIEND
DOYUN'S YOUNGER SISTER?

702
00:27:01,829 --> 00:27:03,204
[Lee Hyunsoo] Park Taeo's girlfriend.

703
00:27:03,205 --> 00:27:05,957
The fan club ledger we saw earlier

704
00:27:05,958 --> 00:27:07,959
was written by Kim Doyeon.

705
00:27:07,960 --> 00:27:09,669
And your name is Kim Doyun.

706
00:27:09,670 --> 00:27:11,379
Isn't that a bit of a stretch?

707
00:27:11,380 --> 00:27:12,547
How so?

708
00:27:12,548 --> 00:27:14,508
The name "Doyeon"
has appeared a few times.

709
00:27:15,134 --> 00:27:17,051
I don't have a younger sibling.
I'm an only child.

710
00:27:17,052 --> 00:27:19,679
- You seem to be hiding something.
- [Kim Doyun] I'm not.

711
00:27:19,680 --> 00:27:22,640
You seem to be hiding something
whenever we come back to this topic.

712
00:27:22,641 --> 00:27:24,058
Not at all.

713
00:27:24,059 --> 00:27:25,434
You seem to keep changing the topic.

714
00:27:25,435 --> 00:27:28,229
I don't know if I should say this, but--

715
00:27:28,230 --> 00:27:30,690
You keep turning it around on me.

716
00:27:30,691 --> 00:27:32,191
We're not trying to pin it on you.

717
00:27:32,192 --> 00:27:34,402
- Let me share what I know.
- Okay.

718
00:27:34,403 --> 00:27:37,238
- The name is Kim Doyeon, right?
- Yes.

719
00:27:37,239 --> 00:27:38,656
- Kim Doyeon.
- Yes.

720
00:27:38,657 --> 00:27:41,493
- She's actually someone I know.
- Ah.

721
00:27:42,244 --> 00:27:43,995
[Jo Hajun] Kim Doyeon.

722
00:27:43,996 --> 00:27:47,582
- We went to middle school together.
- Okay.

723
00:27:47,583 --> 00:27:48,834
Kim Doyeon.

724
00:27:50,043 --> 00:27:51,712
Based on the information I know,

725
00:27:52,337 --> 00:27:55,299
you're her older brother.

726
00:27:55,841 --> 00:27:56,842
What?

727
00:27:57,968 --> 00:27:59,176
Are you Doyeon's brother?

728
00:27:59,177 --> 00:28:01,220
- No. I don't have a sister.
- Is she your younger sister?

729
00:28:01,221 --> 00:28:02,890
- What?
- I don't have a sister.

730
00:28:03,932 --> 00:28:05,349
- Who's lying?
- Are you in your right mind?

731
00:28:05,350 --> 00:28:06,476
- Someone's lying.
- I'm not.

732
00:28:07,561 --> 00:28:09,103
Are you lying right now?

733
00:28:09,104 --> 00:28:10,313
- You do have a sister!
- Come on.

734
00:28:10,314 --> 00:28:11,689
- I really don't.
- Hang on.

735
00:28:11,690 --> 00:28:13,232
She was my schoolmate.

736
00:28:13,233 --> 00:28:15,818
<i>-We went to school together.
- Okay.</i>

737
00:28:15,819 --> 00:28:18,279
DID KIM DOYEON AND JO HAJUN
GO TO THE SAME SCHOOL?

738
00:28:18,280 --> 00:28:21,365
- From what I know…
- Yes?

739
00:28:21,366 --> 00:28:23,576
…Kim Doyeon was the original
president of the fan club.

740
00:28:23,577 --> 00:28:25,328
DOYEON WAS
THE ORIGINAL PRESIDENT?

741
00:28:25,329 --> 00:28:27,748
- She was the original president.
- Yes.

742
00:28:28,332 --> 00:28:30,374
I don't know if I should say this,

743
00:28:30,375 --> 00:28:31,459
but Kim Doyeon died.

744
00:28:31,460 --> 00:28:32,668
FORMER PRESIDENT IS DEAD?

745
00:28:32,669 --> 00:28:35,422
- She died, and--
- Why are there so many dead people?

746
00:28:36,298 --> 00:28:38,257
It's my understanding
that the person who took over

747
00:28:38,258 --> 00:28:41,385
as the new president of the fan club
was Kim Doyun.

748
00:28:41,386 --> 00:28:42,803
So what was your relationship with her?

749
00:28:42,804 --> 00:28:46,641
Doyeon and I went to the same school.

750
00:28:46,642 --> 00:28:48,517
<i>When I was first assigned
to the promotion campaign,</i>

751
00:28:48,518 --> 00:28:52,271
<i>she recommended Park Taeo
and connected me to him.</i>

752
00:28:52,272 --> 00:28:55,900
<i>But for some unknown reason,
she took her own life.</i>

753
00:28:55,901 --> 00:28:57,610
Someone with a similar name

754
00:28:57,611 --> 00:29:01,949
suddenly took over
as president of the same fan club.

755
00:29:02,574 --> 00:29:05,576
It's so strange that he was
her immediate successor.

756
00:29:05,577 --> 00:29:09,622
You knew that Park Taeo
had something to do

757
00:29:09,623 --> 00:29:11,958
with the death of the first president
of the fan club.

758
00:29:11,959 --> 00:29:13,334
[Kim Doyun] Mmm.

759
00:29:13,335 --> 00:29:17,630
Then I guess the private post
could've been written by Kim Doyeon.

760
00:29:17,631 --> 00:29:19,548
- It seems like we all had a motive.
- Yeah.

761
00:29:19,549 --> 00:29:21,842
We all had a motive.

762
00:29:21,843 --> 00:29:23,803
- We all have a story.
- What's more important

763
00:29:23,804 --> 00:29:24,888
is who struck Taeo last.

764
00:29:25,389 --> 00:29:27,473
If we focus on the timing,

765
00:29:27,474 --> 00:29:29,642
- you went in as I left, right?
- Yeah.

766
00:29:29,643 --> 00:29:31,686
- That was around 11:05 p.m., right?
- Yes.

767
00:29:31,687 --> 00:29:33,062
When did you say you left?

768
00:29:33,063 --> 00:29:35,106
I went in at 11:05 p.m.
and left about 15 minutes later.

769
00:29:35,107 --> 00:29:36,732
What time did you say you went in?

770
00:29:36,733 --> 00:29:38,693
- Be honest.
- It was 11:30 p.m.

771
00:29:38,694 --> 00:29:40,861
So between 11:15 and 11:30 p.m.,

772
00:29:40,862 --> 00:29:42,405
Park Taeo was knocked out.

773
00:29:42,406 --> 00:29:44,782
- Right?
- Yeah, however it happened.

774
00:29:44,783 --> 00:29:47,284
Right. I thought he was dead,

775
00:29:47,285 --> 00:29:49,829
but whether he was actually dead

776
00:29:49,830 --> 00:29:52,623
or if he was just struck
and fainted from hypoglycemia

777
00:29:52,624 --> 00:29:54,542
- is undetermined.
- We don't know exactly.

778
00:29:54,543 --> 00:29:58,295
But we know for sure that he was
knocked out because he was hit

779
00:29:58,296 --> 00:30:00,297
- or because he ate the cake.
- He was struck.

780
00:30:00,298 --> 00:30:01,632
- He definitely ate the cake.
- Right.

781
00:30:01,633 --> 00:30:04,677
Whether it was the cake or a beating
or his head slamming into something,

782
00:30:04,678 --> 00:30:07,430
- we know it happened in the locker room.
- Yes.

783
00:30:07,431 --> 00:30:08,724
Then aren't you the prime suspect?

784
00:30:09,307 --> 00:30:11,934
Wait. Hear me out. The reason I told you--

785
00:30:11,935 --> 00:30:13,102
So whether he's lying or--

786
00:30:13,103 --> 00:30:15,312
I didn't need to tell you,
and I knew you would suspect me,

787
00:30:15,313 --> 00:30:17,898
but I told you anyway
because it was the only way

788
00:30:17,899 --> 00:30:19,567
you'd know for sure it wasn't me.

789
00:30:19,568 --> 00:30:22,570
He was unconscious when I found him,
so he was either already dead or…

790
00:30:22,571 --> 00:30:24,155
I thought he was dead.

791
00:30:24,156 --> 00:30:26,907
But seeing this made me think
he might've died later.

792
00:30:26,908 --> 00:30:30,119
And I shared what should've been a secret
to make that point.

793
00:30:30,120 --> 00:30:32,121
- So when it comes to suspecting--
- [timer beeping]

794
00:30:32,122 --> 00:30:33,414
- What?
- Is that the end?

795
00:30:33,415 --> 00:30:34,999
Does that mean we're screwed?

796
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:37,085
You were all convinced it was me
at the start.

797
00:30:37,836 --> 00:30:40,004
- What the heck?
- [Kang Dohyun] Talk about ridiculous.

798
00:30:40,005 --> 00:30:41,922
I think the manager
got into a fight with Taeo.

799
00:30:41,923 --> 00:30:44,633
[host] <i>Before voting,
please make your closing arguments.</i>

800
00:30:44,634 --> 00:30:47,803
- Sure, I'm not entirely innocent.
- [players laughing]

801
00:30:47,804 --> 00:30:49,847
I've committed a few blunders.

802
00:30:49,848 --> 00:30:52,391
But I've been wrongly accused.
I'm not the killer.

803
00:30:52,392 --> 00:30:55,311
You may suspect me because of the cake,

804
00:30:55,312 --> 00:30:57,104
but you saw the medical record earlier.

805
00:30:57,105 --> 00:31:00,649
Can the immediate cause of death
be attributed to me?

806
00:31:00,650 --> 00:31:03,736
I did plan to kill him, but I didn't.
I never even hit him.

807
00:31:03,737 --> 00:31:06,906
I think the answer
lies in the time of his death.

808
00:31:06,907 --> 00:31:09,658
I want you to look for the person
who could've been there at that time.

809
00:31:09,659 --> 00:31:10,993
I'll pass.

810
00:31:10,994 --> 00:31:12,912
You don't need to defend yourself, huh?

811
00:31:12,913 --> 00:31:15,998
The fan club president is Kim Doyun,
but there was a Kim Doyeon.

812
00:31:15,999 --> 00:31:20,211
I figured it could be related
to a sibling connection,

813
00:31:20,212 --> 00:31:22,713
<i>so the fan club president
was my prime suspect until the end.</i>

814
00:31:22,714 --> 00:31:26,175
I think I'm leaning towards the coach
as my final guess

815
00:31:26,176 --> 00:31:29,553
because the timeline
makes him the most likely suspect.

816
00:31:29,554 --> 00:31:32,098
Coach Yoon isn't a big guy,

817
00:31:32,099 --> 00:31:37,144
so he weakened Taeo with the cake,
then struck him with the bat.

818
00:31:37,145 --> 00:31:40,523
<i>As awful as it is,
I think that's how it went down.</i>

819
00:31:40,524 --> 00:31:43,442
VOTING COMPLETE

820
00:31:43,443 --> 00:31:45,986
[host] <i>Here are the voting results.</i>

821
00:31:45,987 --> 00:31:47,488
<i>Kang Dohyun got zero votes,</i>

822
00:31:47,489 --> 00:31:48,739
<i>Lee Hyunsoo got zero votes,</i>

823
00:31:48,740 --> 00:31:49,824
<i>Jo Hajun got zero votes,</i>

824
00:31:49,825 --> 00:31:51,325
<i>Yoon Minseok got two votes,</i>

825
00:31:51,326 --> 00:31:52,536
<i>and Kim Doyun got three votes.</i>

826
00:31:53,036 --> 00:31:55,079
<i>Kim Doyun got the most votes.</i>

827
00:31:55,080 --> 00:31:57,832
SIGH

828
00:31:57,833 --> 00:32:02,378
[host] <i>The selected player shall open
the ending box bearing their number</i>

829
00:32:02,379 --> 00:32:05,965
<i>and read the ending scenario aloud.</i>

830
00:32:05,966 --> 00:32:09,218
I can't believe you're making me
do something so humiliating.

831
00:32:09,219 --> 00:32:12,972
"Doyun insisted it was revenge
for his younger sister, Doyeon."

832
00:32:12,973 --> 00:32:15,349
<i>"After losing his parents in a car crash,</i>

833
00:32:15,350 --> 00:32:17,101
<i>the only family he had left was Doyeon."</i>

834
00:32:17,102 --> 00:32:20,437
<i>"When he found out that Park Taeo
had abandoned his sister,</i>

835
00:32:20,438 --> 00:32:22,274
<i>he made up his mind to get revenge."</i>

836
00:32:22,774 --> 00:32:24,191
<i>"Jo Hajun's victory cake,</i>

837
00:32:24,192 --> 00:32:26,235
<i>the insulin and glucose
discarded by the manager,</i>

838
00:32:26,236 --> 00:32:28,445
<i>and Lee Hyunsoo's ball toss</i>

839
00:32:28,446 --> 00:32:30,991
<i>all contributed to Park Taeo's death."</i>

840
00:32:31,575 --> 00:32:34,785
<i>"However, it was Doyun
who delivered the fatal blow with a bat."</i>

841
00:32:34,786 --> 00:32:36,787
NAILED IT!

842
00:32:36,788 --> 00:32:38,747
THE CULPRIT WAS KIM DOYUN

843
00:32:38,748 --> 00:32:41,041
- I was right!
- I knew it.

844
00:32:41,042 --> 00:32:42,293
"Kim Doyun's fate."

845
00:32:42,294 --> 00:32:44,420
<i>"He confessed everything
as soon as he was named the culprit."</i>

846
00:32:44,421 --> 00:32:46,255
<i>"He was arrested
and imprisoned for murder,</i>

847
00:32:46,256 --> 00:32:48,674
<i>but his mental state
deteriorated before the trial."</i>

848
00:32:48,675 --> 00:32:51,595
<i>"By order of the court,
he was placed in a psychiatric ward."</i>

849
00:32:52,220 --> 00:32:54,346
- Do I need to read it all?
- It's public humiliation.

850
00:32:54,347 --> 00:32:55,931
It's humiliating.

851
00:32:55,932 --> 00:32:57,641
He needs to expose himself.

852
00:32:57,642 --> 00:33:00,060
Why do I need to read out
everything I did?

853
00:33:00,061 --> 00:33:01,605
Can't you just put this in the captions?

854
00:33:02,856 --> 00:33:05,441
- Or present it as a slideshow.
- Can't I read it for him?

855
00:33:05,442 --> 00:33:08,652
<i>"It turned out to be
a bereaved family's anguished cry."</i>

856
00:33:08,653 --> 00:33:12,239
<i>"But the law made no allowance
for the tragic circumstances."</i>

857
00:33:12,240 --> 00:33:13,699
<i>"Due to his mental breakdown,</i>

858
00:33:13,700 --> 00:33:16,493
<i>he was put in a treatment facility
instead of being imprisoned."</i>

859
00:33:16,494 --> 00:33:18,704
<i>"Rather than just a murderer,</i>

860
00:33:18,705 --> 00:33:20,957
<i>he was remembered as a victim
who lost his sister."</i>

861
00:33:23,460 --> 00:33:27,005
THE FULL STORY

862
00:33:28,673 --> 00:33:30,383
22:30 THE SAINTS VICTORY

863
00:33:30,967 --> 00:33:32,844
I hurt a friend in my youth.

864
00:33:34,012 --> 00:33:36,723
I resolved to take baseball seriously
from that day onward.

865
00:33:44,439 --> 00:33:46,690
[Jo Hajun]
Please pass this on to Lee Hyunsoo.

866
00:33:46,691 --> 00:33:49,903
22:45 JO HAJUN DELIVERS THE CAKE

867
00:33:54,491 --> 00:33:57,201
22:50 KANG DOHYUN THROWS AWAY
THE INSULIN AND GLUCOSE GEL

868
00:33:57,202 --> 00:33:58,203
Congratulations.

869
00:33:58,787 --> 00:34:01,622
22:55 KIM DOYUN VISITS THE LOCKER ROOM

870
00:34:01,623 --> 00:34:02,832
Thank you.

871
00:34:08,046 --> 00:34:09,797
23:00 KIM DOYUN'S MURDER ATTEMPT FAILS

872
00:34:09,798 --> 00:34:11,173
COACH'S OFFICE

873
00:34:11,174 --> 00:34:14,301
23:05 YOON MINSEOK
FINDS A REPORT

874
00:34:14,302 --> 00:34:16,263
ABOUT HIS SON'S DEATH

875
00:34:17,764 --> 00:34:20,767
23:05 LEE HYUNSOO ENTERS

876
00:34:22,727 --> 00:34:24,145
We need to talk, Park Taeo!

877
00:34:24,729 --> 00:34:27,148
[pants, groans]

878
00:34:27,857 --> 00:34:29,483
Let's talk later, Hyunsoo.

879
00:34:29,484 --> 00:34:32,028
I want to talk now!

880
00:34:34,072 --> 00:34:35,740
I said let's talk later.

881
00:34:37,409 --> 00:34:39,160
Are you looking down on me?

882
00:34:40,245 --> 00:34:41,246
[grunts]

883
00:34:52,173 --> 00:34:55,093
23:30 YOON MINSEOK
ENTERS THE LOCKER ROOM

884
00:34:56,886 --> 00:34:58,388
[phone rings]

885
00:34:59,931 --> 00:35:01,432
Did you deliver the cake?

886
00:35:01,433 --> 00:35:02,725
<i>Yes, it's been delivered.</i>

887
00:35:02,726 --> 00:35:05,269
<i>An article's going to run
about Park Taeo's upcoming marriage.</i>

888
00:35:05,270 --> 00:35:06,979
<i>He's dated her for a year.</i>

889
00:35:06,980 --> 00:35:08,063
23:35 DOYUN LEARNS TAEO CHEATED

890
00:35:08,064 --> 00:35:10,733
23:40 HE GOES BACK
TO THE LOCKER ROOM

891
00:35:10,734 --> 00:35:12,152
[Taeo] My blood sugar level is low.

892
00:35:12,736 --> 00:35:14,821
Bring me the glucose gel from my bag.

893
00:35:17,699 --> 00:35:18,700
Hey.

894
00:35:21,036 --> 00:35:22,953
Do you know why Doyeon died?

895
00:35:22,954 --> 00:35:24,998
No, I don't.

896
00:35:25,707 --> 00:35:26,750
You don't?

897
00:36:05,497 --> 00:36:07,499
Translated by Hannah Og Nam
